<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Molteno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1886">1886</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir John Charles Molteno</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir John Charles Molteno was a London-born Cape merchant and farmer who led the campaign for responsible government and became the first prime minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> in 1872. His government built railways and resisted the British plan for a confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, and he was dismissed by Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartle-frere">Sir Bartle Frere</a> in 1878.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-molteno.jpg" alt="John Molteno" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Walker &amp; Boutall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Molteno_Cropped.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
